Z||000000||johnmac||09-01-2001||03:35 PM||||Finally installed my rebuilt alternator into my V6 Automatic --- what a bear! I installed new brushes and diodes.<P>Just hooked up the big one wire post of the Alternator and I have shorted out entire electrical system. The + & - are connected via this one wire connection.<P>HELP - IS THIS A BAD ALTERNATOR OR WHAT.<P>HELPPPPPPPP!!!<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||09-01-2001||10:41 PM||||sounds like when you were putting in the screws that hold down the voltage regulator and diode bridge/trio some have plastic insulating washers and some don't, to insolate against the case.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnmac||09-01-2001||11:35 PM||||I disconnected the wire to the alternator and found that this wire was the source.<P>Alternator is okay.<P>Now unraveling the wire loom and tracing the line back to the source.<P>Nothing on this Fiero is ever simple!!!<P>Last car I restored from the ground up was a Jaq XK120 and that was simple.<P>This Fiero is definitely a challenge!<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
